    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpTitle">Help &amp; Documentation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpHeader">Help Center</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSubHeader">Find important information and practical examples on how to use the application.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection1Title">1. Create Macro &amp; Learn Keys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection1Text" xml:space="preserve">• Click "+ New" at the bottom left to add a command.
• Use the scan mode to automatically capture keys from your couch keyboard.
• Name your macro and manage existing commands via the selection list.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection2Title">2. Open Apps &amp; Focus Windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection2Text" xml:space="preserve">Enter the path to an application or use smart focus commands to bring existing windows to the foreground instead of reopening them.
• Focus{Kodi} – Brings Kodi to the screen.
• Focus{firefox} / Focus{Thunderbird} – Switches to browser or mail.
• Focus{explorer} – Opens Windows Explorer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection3Title">3. Keyboard Shortcuts &amp; Media Control</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection3Text" xml:space="preserve">Use your keyboard like a remote control for your PC:
• %{TAB} – Fast task switching (Alt+Tab).
• {SPACE} – Play or pause media (Spacebar).
• %{F4} – Closes the active window immediately (Alt+F4).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection4Title">4. Customizing Appearance &amp; Language</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection4Text" xml:space="preserve">Customize the theme in the top right corner – ideal for home theaters or matching Windows system mode. 
You can also change the user interface language flexibly at any time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection5Title">5. Security, Backup &amp; Autostart</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="StrHelpSection5Text" xml:space="preserve">Backup your macros as a JSON file or import existing configurations. 
Activate the lightning icon in the title bar for Windows autostart so the app runs quietly in the background as a tray icon.</sys:String>
